3) Root Cause  
The root cause is that the class implements the Cloneable interface and exposes the default `clone()` method, which performs a shallow copy of the object. This cloning process copies all fields, including sensitive information, without any safeguards, increasing the risk of accidental data exposure or improper handling of sensitive data during cloning.

4) Impact  
- Unintended data disclosure if cloned objects are exposed or logged.  
- Leakage of confidential data during object duplication.  
