- Avoid cloning objects that contain sensitive information or implement custom clone methods that do not copy sensitive fields.  
- Use explicit copying methods that omit or securely handle sensitive data.  
- Consider making sensitive fields transient or encrypting them to prevent accidental exposure during cloning.  
- Review design to ensure sensitive data is not duplicated or transmitted unnecessarily.  
- Implement secure serialization/deserialization practices if object persistence or transfer is necessary.

