    }
}

Vulnerability Report

1. Vulnerability Description
The code demonstrates a security-critical validation process that can be optimized away by the compiler due to the use of a local variable that is only written once and then immediately checked. This optimization can potentially remove essential validation logic, leading to situations where invalid tokens are mistakenly accepted or valid tokens are not properly validated, exposing the system to security risks.

