// 9. Simplistic type coercion in age validation
public class AgeValidator {
    public boolean isAdult(Object ageObj) {
        int age = 0;
        if (ageObj instanceof String) {
            try {
                age = Integer.parseInt((String) ageObj);
            } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
                return false;
            }
        } else if (ageObj instanceof Integer) {
            age = (Integer) ageObj;
        } else {
            return false;
        }
        return age >= 18;
    }
}

Vulnerability Report

1) Vulnerability Description:
The code exhibits CWE-192: Integer Coercion Error, which arises from unsafe or improper handling of integer values during type conversion. This can lead to incorrect age validation if malicious or malformed input is provided, potentially allowing underage users to bypass age restrictions.

