// 3. Index validation with incorrect upper bound check
public class Example3 {
    public void getElement(String userInput) {
        int[] numbers = {100, 200, 300, 400};
        int index = Integer.parseInt(userInput);
        // Incorrect validation: allowing index == length
        if (index >= 0 && index <= numbers.length) {
            System.out.println("Number: " + numbers[index]);
        } else {
            System.out.println("Invalid index");
        }
    }
}

VULNERABILITY REPORT

1. Vulnerability Description
The provided Java code contains an Improper Validation of Array Index (CWE-129). Specifically, the index validation logic incorrectly allows an index value equal to the array's length, which leads to an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException at runtime. This improper validation can cause program crashes or unintended behavior.

2. Vulnerable Code
```java
