The validation logic uses `index <= numbers.length`, which permits `index` to be equal to the length of the array. Since Java arrays are zero-indexed, valid indices range from 0 to `length - 1`. Allowing `index == length` leads to an attempt to access an array element outside of valid bounds, causing an `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException`.

