**Summary**

This code demonstrates a CWE-170-like vulnerability by neglecting null termination in a simulated C string context within Java. Proper null termination is essential when interoperating with native code or systems reliant on C-style string conventions to prevent undefined behavior and enhance security.

// 10. Using ByteBuffer without explicit null termination, potentially leading to improper string handling
import java.nio.ByteBuffer;

public class VulnerableExample10 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
