### 3) Root Cause

The root cause of the vulnerability is the absence of braces `{}` in the `if` statement. In Java, if braces are omitted, only the next single statement is considered part of the `if`. This misleads maintainers to assume all subsequent code is guarded by the condition, which is not the case here.

**Incorrect:**
```java
if (condition)
    statement1;
statement2; // runs unconditionally
```

**Correct:**
```java
if (condition) {
    statement1;
    statement2; // both guarded
}
```

In the provided code, this oversight leads to login attempt messages and access grants being executed independently, potentially causing security lapses or logical errors.

---

### 4) Impact

