  } else {
      // Handle out-of-range values appropriately
      throw new ArithmeticException("Value out of range for short");
  }
  ```
- Optionally, round or truncate the float value explicitly to control how fractional parts are handled.
- Implement input validation and proper exception handling to manage values outside range.
- Consider alternative data types if higher range or precision is necessary.

---

*By validating input and handling potential overflow conditions, developers can prevent numeric truncation errors and enhance application security and correctness.*

