// 5. Caching system that allocates cache entries repeatedly without total memory restriction
public class CacheSystem {
    private static final int MAX_CACHE_SIZE = 500_000_000; // bytes
    private int currentCacheSize = 0;
    private List<byte[]> cacheEntries = new ArrayList<>();

    public void addCacheEntries(int numberOfEntries, int sizePerEntry) {
        for (int i = 0; i < numberOfEntries; i++) {
            if (currentCacheSize + sizePerEntry > MAX_CACHE_SIZE) {
                break; // No limit handling
            }
            byte[] entry = new byte[sizePerEntry];
            cacheEntries.add(entry);
            currentCacheSize += sizePerEntry;
        }
    }
}

Vulnerability Report

1) Vulnerability Description:
The provided Java code exhibits a vulnerability related to improper control over sequential memory allocation. Specifically, it repeatedly allocates large cache entries without a comprehensive check for total memory usage, risking uncontrolled consumption of system memory and potential out-of-memory errors.

2) Vulnerable Code:
```java
