1) Vulnerability Description
The code contains a sign extension vulnerability (CWE-194), which occurs when a signed byte value is implicitly converted to an int, potentially preserving its negative sign. When this value is used as an array index, it can lead to unexpected behaviors such as accessing invalid indices, resulting in runtime exceptions or security issues.

