The root cause is the implicit conversion of the signed `byte` (`indexByte`) to an `int`. Because `byte` in Java ranges from -128 to 127, negative values can be sign-extended when converted to `int`. Using such negative indices directly to access array elements can cause `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` or unintended behavior.

