// 1. Using Runtime.exec() to execute system commands directly from user input
public class CommandInjection1 {
    public void executeCommand(String userInput) {
        try {
            String command = "ls " + userInput; // Potentially dangerous
            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}

**Vulnerability Report**

---

### 1. Vulnerability Description
The code demonstrates a command injection vulnerability due to the use of `Runtime.exec()` with unvalidated user input. An attacker can craft input to execute arbitrary system commands, potentially compromising the system's stability, security, or data integrity.

---

### 2. Vulnerable Code
```java
public class CommandInjection1 {
    public void executeCommand(String userInput) {
        try {
            String command = "ls " + userInput; // Potentially dangerous
            Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```

