The code uses path normalization without validating or constraining the length of the resulting path. This can lead to buffer overflows or resource exhaustion if an attacker supplies an excessively long or maliciously crafted input path. This scenario aligns with CWE-785: Use of Path Manipulation Function without Maximum-sized Buffer, where the function assumes the path fits into a predefined buffer size without proper validation.

